I’ll inspect the pattern, metadata, and the provided PXRD workflow guidance first, then index/search candidate phases and carry the strongest model through GSAS-II refinement. I’ll keep the structural assignments and quantitative fractions tied to explicit fit evidence, and flag anything the data cannot support.

The chemistry strongly suggests Ca–W–O products, but at 800 °C a nominal 1:1 charge does not by itself prove single-phase CaWO₄. I’m now extracting peak positions and checking the case-specific COD library so residual WO₃/CaO or calcium-rich intermediates are tested rather than assumed away.

Peak matching now supports three crystalline components: scheelite CaWO₄, monoclinic WO₃, and rock-salt CaO. The weak CaO lines at about 32.11°, 37.44°, 53.41°, 64.38°, and 67.37° are especially diagnostic; I’m screening the closely related monoclinic WO₃ references by whole-profile refinement before fixing the model.

