The final model now reaches Rwp ≈3.601%. Scheelite itself shows no measurable texture; a weak but statistically supported [111] texture term belongs to Ca₃WO₆ (March ratio 0.963). The remaining largest residuals are shape/position differences with matched integrated areas, not evidence for a fourth crystalline phase. I’m freezing this model and validating an independent forward replay before writing the deliverables.

